#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:6
msgid "Rust Binaries"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:8
msgid ""
"Let's start with a simple application. At the root of an AOSP checkout, "
"create the following files:"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:11
msgid "_hello_rust/Android.bp_:"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:15 src/android/build-rules/binary.md:16
msgid "\"hello_rust\""
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:17
msgid "\"src/main.rs\""
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:21
msgid "_hello_rust/src/main.rs_:"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:24
msgid "// Copyright 2022 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:25
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:26
msgid "//! Rust demo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:28
msgid "/// Prints a greeting to standard output.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:31
msgid "\"Hello from Rust!\""
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:35
msgid "You can now build, push, and run the binary:"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:37
msgid ""
"```shell\n"
"m hello_rust\n"
"adb push \"$ANDROID_PRODUCT_OUT/system/bin/hello_rust\" /data/local/tmp\n"
"adb shell /data/local/tmp/hello_rust\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:49
msgid ""
"Go through the build steps and demonstrate them running in your emulator."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:51
msgid ""
"Notice the extensive documentation comments? The Android build rules enforce "
"that all modules have documentation. Try removing it and see what error you "
"get."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules/binary.md:55
msgid ""
"Stress that the Rust build rules look like the other Soong rules. This is by "
"design, to make using Rust as easy as C++ or Java."
msgstr ""
